@page "/privacy"
@model Site.Pages.PrivacyModel
<div class="container narrow">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
        Document Number Validator is a documentation and demo site for an open-source .NET library.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
        This site uses Google Analytics (Google tag, measurement ID <code>G-972WK5CM96</code>) to understand
        how the site is used — for example, which pages are visited and how visitors arrive. Google Analytics
        sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_gid</code>) and collects data including your IP
        address, browser and device information, and the pages you view. This data is processed by Google and
        may be transferred to and stored on servers outside your country.
    </p>
    <p>
        No advertising or marketing trackers are used. You can opt out of Google Analytics by installing the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser
        Add-on</a>, blocking analytics scripts, or using your browser's Do Not Track / tracking-protection
        settings. See the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        The only first-party browser storage used is your colour-theme preference (<code>localStorage</code>),
        which never leaves your device. The analytics cookies described above are set by Google Analytics if
        you accept them through your browser's settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Demo inputs</h2>
    <p>
        Values you enter in the on-page demo are processed in memory on the server for the current request
        so that validation can run. They are not persisted, logged to the application data store or shared
        with third parties. Do not enter real personal or financial data into the demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
        As with any hosted website, the hosting provider may keep standard infrastructure logs (such as IP
        address, requested URL and timestamp) for security and operations purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
        The website source and the validator libraries are public on
        <a href="@SiteInfo.WebsiteRepositoryUrl" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. If you have questions or want to
        request a change, open an issue.
    </p>
</div>
